Subject: [PATCH 11255/11362] Close the 7033 review: one producer edit replaces
 findings 1 and 9

The reviewer's best contribution is not a finding, it is noticing that two of them
share a cause. Findings 1 and 9 both leak because the reader derives level-scoped
facts from run-level aggregates. Both vanish if the window row records a monotone
stretch id and the enabled set as of that window, making the exhaustion test
row-local. One producer edit instead of two reader patches; round four is asked
to build that rather than nine fixes.

Also records why the replay validation is trusted. The reviewer falsified it
rather than confirming it: breaking the reconstruction two different ways gave 0
of 6 rows validating each time, and unmutated all 6 validate and reproduce the
table. A check that only ever agrees is not a check.

And a subtlety worth copying from its mutation spot-check: it verified every
replacement was syntactically valid, so that no mutation could go RED from a
SyntaxError rather than from the deleted rule. A RED for the wrong reason proves
nothing.

