+### Review closed 13:48Z — one fix replaces two findings; round four dispatched
+
+**Findings 1 and 9 have the SAME resolution, and it is a better change than either patch.**
+Both leak because the READER derives level-scoped facts from run-level aggregates. Both vanish if
+`_record_unredirected_window` records the state on the ROW: a monotone stretch id alongside the
+raw `level` (kills finding 1), and `enabled_arms()` evaluated at the same moment as `arms_used`
+(kills finding 9). The exhaustion test then becomes purely row-local and neither axis can leak
+across levels. One producer edit instead of two reader patches. The reviewer proposed it; I agree
+and it is what round four is asked to build.
+
+**Ranking, from the reviewer:** finding 1 is LIVE — it needs only a level-counter decrease, which
+the recorded corpus already contains. Finding 9 is LATENT — it needs a mid-run flip of
+`CARNOT_ARC_SUPERVISOR_TOOL_ARM`. Not contrived: SCENARIO-ARC-WMTE-7030-B exists precisely for
+that flip.
+
+**The replay validation is EARNED, and the reviewer proved it by falsification rather than
+agreement.** It broke the reconstruction two ways — `window + 1`, and shifting the level-up offset
+from `frame_index + 1` to `frame_index` — and got 0 of 6 rows validating each time. Unmutated all
+6 validate and reproduce the table exactly: 4/4/3/3/4 exhausted windows on level 0, 18 total, 0 on
+any deeper level, level 0 cleared at 885/885/771/885/888/885. A check that only ever agrees is not
+a check; this one was shown able to fail.
+
+**Mutation spot-check by the reviewer:** M4 and M12 re-run, both RED, both restored
+byte-identical, `git status` clean after. Anchors are call sites or producer writes, not literal
+defaults. It also checked every replacement for SYNTAX VALIDITY so that no mutation could go RED
+from a `SyntaxError` rather than from the rule — a subtlety worth copying, because a syntax error
+produces a RED that proves nothing.
+
+**Record integrity confirmed independently:** `git diff --name-only bd46ce7e65 HEAD` touches only
+`docs/ openspec/ ops/ python/ tests/` — nothing under `results/`. The ledger matches the previous
+HEAD key-by-key on `controls`, `created_at`, all 14 `entries` and `schema`; only `recommendation`
+and `updated_at` differ. REQ-7033 itself agrees with the code exactly, and every 7033 scenario has
+a test that names it. The spec/code disagreements are confined to the requirements 7033 amended,
+which is finding 2.
+
+**Round four dispatched to the agent that owns the file, not to the reviewer.** DECISION 17 stays
+NO until it lands. DECISION 18 is unaffected and still open.
 
 
